  "proof": "Nonnegative weights make the score nondecreasing in each utility: its positive-ideal complement distance decreases and negative-ideal distance increases. Fixed U makes exclusive regret R_i=max(0,max_{k != i} U_k-L_i); increasing a target lower score affects only its own regret. At the joint endpoint both target regrets exceed the unchanged non-target winner; other competitors are unchanged. Every possible-champion inequality U_i>=max_{k != i} L_k holds at the joint endpoint, so it holds throughout the box. Every necessary inequality L_i>=max_{k != i} U_k fails at that endpoint, so it fails throughout, since all L_i elsewhere are no larger. Comparisons use model tolerance 1e-12. Exclusive regret follows independent city intervals; if i is itself the maximal upper, including its own U would overstate attainable regret.",
